# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Horizontal/Vertical takes the other direction when only that can be
# added (mitcad#2184), on sketch-horizontal-vertical-other.json's Sketch1:
# the fixed point p1 (-10, 6) and p2 (10, 0) held on the fixed
# construction line along y = 0; 1 degree of freedom. The points are
# nearer to level, which their held heights conflict with.
#   1. Horizontal/Vertical (Shift+V), p1, then the pointer on p2: the
#      glyph by the cursor is plumb (`vertical_points`).
#   2. The click adds a vertical alignment, no refusal; p2 slides under p1
#      to (-10, 0) and the sketch is fully constrained.
#   3. One undo step takes it away.
# The clicks stay within x -30..30 mm, y -25..25 mm: the free part of the
# view after the fit, also in session 0's 1024x768 window on Windows. Run
# by tools/ui-sketch-horizontal-vertical-other-test.sh (Linux),
# tools/ui-windows-sketch-horizontal-vertical-other-test.ps1 (Windows) and
# tools/ui-macos-sketch-horizontal-vertical-other-test.sh (macOS).
expect-ever 'View area'
wait-idle
expect-ever '^Timeline Sketch1 at '
mark
dblclick-logged '^Timeline Sketch1 at '
wait-log '^Editing sketch F1 \(Sketch1\)' 30
wait-log '^Sketch Sketch1: 1 DOF$'
key F6
wait-idle
capture-undo-depth baseline

# 1. The tool, p1, then the pointer on p2: plumb is what it would add.
mark
key shift+v
wait-log '^Sketch tool Horizontal/Vertical$'
sketch-click -10 6
sketch-move 10 0
wait-log '^Horizontal/Vertical would add vertical_points on p1, p2$'
screenshot '${MITCAD_TEST_WORK}/sketch-horizontal-vertical-other-hover.png'

# 2. The click: plumb, not refused.
sketch-click 10 0
wait-log '^Horizontal/Vertical: horizontal_points on p1, p2 cannot be added; vertical_points instead$'
wait-log '^Added constraint vertical_points k[0-9]+ on p1, p2$'
wait-log '^Sketch Sketch1: 0 DOF, fully constrained$'
expect-no-log 'Horizontal/Vertical not added|does not take'
key Escape
wait-idle
capture-model-number p2x '{"query":"sketch","uid":"F1"}' entities.1.at.0
expect-near ${p2x} -10 0 0.000001
capture-model-number p2y '{"query":"sketch","uid":"F1"}' entities.1.at.1
expect-near ${p2y} 0 0 0.000001

# 3. One undo step.
expect-undo-depth ${baseline} 1
mark
key ctrl+z
expect-undo-depth ${baseline} 0
wait-log '^Sketch Sketch1: 1 DOF$'

command sketch.finish
wait-log '^Sketch finished'
expect-never 'TestDriver: FAIL'
